    --- - `cell`: The cell's index.
    --- - `cellHeight`: The height of one cell.
    --- - `cellWidth`: The width of one cell.
    --- - `numColumns`: The number of columns in the sheet.
    --- - `numRows`: The number of rows in the sheet.
    ---
    --- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_TextureBase_SetSpriteSheetCell)
    function SetSpriteSheetCell(cell: number | Secret<number>, numRows: number, numColumns: number, cellWidth: number?, cellHeight: number?)
    --- Sets the coordinates for cropping or transforming the texture.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_TextureBase_SetTexCoord)
    function SetTexCoord(left: number | Secret<number>, right: number | Secret<number>, top: number, bottom: number)
    function SetTexCoord(ulX: number, ulY: number, llX: number, llY: number, urX: number, urY: number, lrX: number, lrY: number)
    --- Sets the texel snapping bias for the texture.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_TextureBase_SetTexelSnappingBias)
    function SetTexelSnappingBias(bias: normalizedValue)
    --- Sets the texture to an image.
    ---
    --- **Parameters**
    --- - `textureAsset`: A FileID or the file path to a texture.
    --- - `wrapModeHorizontal`: If `TextureBase:SetHorizTile` is enabled, sets the wrap behavior for pixels with an x coordinate outside the (0, 1) region of the texture coordinate space.
    --- - `wrapModeVertical`: If `TextureBase:SetVertTile` is enabled, sets the wrap behavior for pixels with a y coordinate outside the (0, 1) region of the texture coordinate space.
    ---
    --- **Returns**
    --- - `success`: This always appears to returns `true`, even for invalid FileIDs or parameters.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_TextureBase_SetTexture)
    function SetTexture(textureAsset: (string | number | Secret<string | number>)?, wrapModeHorizontal: (WrapMode | Secret<WrapMode>)?, wrapModeVertical: (WrapMode | Secret<WrapMode>)?, filterMode: (FilterMode | Secret<FilterMode>)?): boolean
    --- Enables nineslice texture rendering using the specified pixel margins.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_TextureBase_SetTextureSliceMargins)
    function SetTextureSliceMargins(left: number, top: number, right: number, bottom: number)
    --- Controls whether the center and sides are Stretched or Tiled when using nineslice texture rendering.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_TextureBase_SetTextureSliceMode)
    function SetTextureSliceMode(sliceMode: number)
    --- Sets whether the texture should tile vertically.
    ---
    --- **Parameters**
    --- - `tiling`: If true, texture coordinates will be adjusted such that each texture pixel takes up one vertical unit within the widget.
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_TextureBase_SetVertTile)
    function SetVertTile(tiling: boolean?)
    --- Sets a vertex offset for the texture.
    ---
    --- **Parameters**
    --- - `vertexIndex`: Defined in Constants.lua
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_TextureBase_SetVertexOffset)
    function SetVertexOffset(vertexIndex: number, offsetX: uiUnit, offsetY: uiUnit)
end

