declare function GetHomePartyInfo(homePlayers: table): table?
--- Returns info for a message in the mailbox.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `index`: the index of the message (ascending from 1).
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `packageIcon`: texture path for package icon if it contains a package (nil otherwise).
--- - `stationeryIcon`: texture path for mail message icon.
--- - `sender`: name of the player who sent the message.
--- - `subject`: the message subject.
--- - `money`: The amount of money attached.
--- - `CODAmount`: The amount of COD payment required to receive the package.
--- - `daysLeft`: The number of days (fractional) before the message expires.
--- - `hasItem`: Either the number of attachments or nil if no items are present. Note that items that have been taken from the mailbox continue to occupy empty slots, but hasItem is the total number of items remaining in the mailbox. Use ATTACHMENTS_MAX_RECEIVE for the total number of attachments rather than this.
--- - `wasRead`: 1 if the mail has been read, nil otherwise. Using GetInboxText() marks an item as read.
--- - `wasReturned`: 1 if the mail was returned, nil otherwise.
--- - `textCreated`: 1 if a letter object has been created from this mail, nil otherwise.
--- - `canReply`: 1 if this letter can be replied to, nil otherwise.
--- - `isGM`: 1 if this letter was sent by a GameMaster.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetInboxHeaderInfo)
declare function GetInboxHeaderInfo(index: number): (string?, string, string, string, number, number, number, number?, boolean?, boolean?, boolean?, boolean?, boolean)
--- Returns info for an auction house invoice.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `index`: The index of the message, starting from 1.
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `invoiceType`: One of "buyer", "seller" or "seller_temp_invoice"; or nil if there is no invoice.
--- - `itemName`: The name of the item sold/bought, or nil if there is no invoice.
--- - `playerName`: The player that sold/bought the item, or nil if there were multiple buyers/sellers involved. Will also return nil if there is no invoice.
--- - `bid`: The amount of money bid on the item.
--- - `buyout`: The amount of money set as buyout for the auction.
--- - `deposit`: The amount paid as deposit for the auction.
--- - `consignment`: The fee charged by the auction house for selling your consignment.
--- - `moneyDelay`: The amount of money that are delayed
--- - `etaHour`: Hour part of the time when delayed auction money will arrive
--- - `etaMin`: Minutes part of the time when delayed auction money will arrive
--- - `count`: Quantity/count of the item in the invoice
--- - `commerceAuction`: True for commerce/commodity auction invoices. Used by Blizzard_MailFrame to hide the purchaser/seller line
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetInboxInvoiceInfo)
declare function GetInboxInvoiceInfo(index: number): (string?, string?, string?, number, number, number, number, number, number, number, number, boolean)
--- Returns info for an item attached to a message in the mailbox.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `index`: The index of the message to query, in the range [1,GetInboxNumItems()]
--- - `itemIndex`: The index of the item to query, in the range [1,ATTACHMENTS_MAX_RECEIVE]
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `name`: The localized name of the item
--- - `itemID`: Numeric ID of the item.
--- - `texture`: The path to the icon texture for the item
--- - `count`: The number of items in the stack
--- - `quality`: The quality index of the item
--- - `canUse`: 1 if the player can use the item, or nil otherwise
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetInboxItem)
declare function GetInboxItem(index: number, itemIndex: number): (string, number, string, number, number, boolean?)
