--- Returns a table with all of the loot info for the current loot window.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetLootInfo)
declare function GetLootInfo(): table[]
--- Returns information about the loot event with rollID.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `rollID`: The number increments by 1 for each new roll. The count is not reset by reloading the UI.
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `texture`: The path of the texture of the item icon.
--- - `name`: The name of the item.
--- - `count`: The quantity of the item.
--- - `quality`: The quality of the item. Starting with 1 for common, going up to 5 for legendary.
--- - `bindOnPickUp`: Returns 1 when the item is bind on pickup, nil otherwise.
--- - `canNeed`: Returns 1 when you can roll need on the item, nil otherwise.
--- - `canGreed`: Returns 1 when you can roll greed on the item, nil otherwise.
--- - `canDisenchant`: Returns 1 when you can disenchant the item, nil otherwise.
--- - `reasonNeed`: See details.
--- - `reasonGreed`: See details.
--- - `reasonDisenchant`: See details.
--- - `deSkillRequired`: Required skill in enchanting to disenchant the item.
--- - `canTransmog`: Returns 1 when you can transmogrify the item, nil otherwise.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetLootRollItemInfo)
declare function GetLootRollItemInfo(rollID: number): (string, string, number, number, boolean?, boolean?, boolean?, boolean?, number, number, number, number, boolean?)
--- Retrieves the itemlink of an item being rolled on.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `id`: id is a number used by the server to keep track of items being rolled on. It is generated server side and transmitted to the client.
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `itemLink`: ItemLink
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetLootRollItemLink)
declare function GetLootRollItemLink(id: number): string
--- <!-- or , , , , --> Summary description.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `rollID`: .
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `timeLeft`: Seconds left in Milliseconds or nil.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetLootRollTimeLeft)
declare function GetLootRollTimeLeft(rollID: number): number?
--- Returns info for a loot slot.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `slot`: the index of the loot (1 is the first item, typically coin)
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `lootIcon`: The path of the graphical icon for the item.
--- - `lootName`: The name of the item.
--- - `lootQuantity`: The quantity of the item in a stack. *Note: Quantity for coin is always 0.*
--- - `currencyID`: The identifying number of the currency loot in slot, if applicable. *Note: Returns nil for slots with coin and regular items.*
--- - `lootQuality`: The Enum.ItemQuality code for the item.
--- - `locked`: Whether you are eligible to loot this item or not. Locked items are by default shown tinted red.
--- - `isQuestItem`: Self-explanatory.
--- - `questID`: The identifying number for the quest.
--- - `isActive`: True if the item starts a quest that you are not currently on.
--- - `isCoin`: True if the slot contains money loot.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetLootSlotInfo)
declare function GetLootSlotInfo(slot: number): (string, string, number, number?, number, boolean, boolean, number, boolean, boolean)
--- Returns the item link for a loot slot.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `index`: The index of the item in the list to retrieve info from (1 to GetNumLootItems())
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `itemLink`: The itemLink for the specified item, or nil if `index` is invalid.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_GetLootSlotLink)
declare function GetLootSlotLink(index: number): string?
--- Returns an integer loot type for a given loot slot.
---
