--- Sets an override key binding.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `owner`: The frame this binding "belongs" to; this can later be used to clear all override bindings belonging to a particular frame.
--- - `isPriority`: true if this is a priority binding, false otherwise. Both types of override bindings take precedence over normal bindings.
--- - `key`: Binding to bind the command to. For example, "Q", "ALT-Q", "ALT-CTRL-SHIFT-Q", "BUTTON5"
--- - `command`: Any name attribute value of a Bindings.xml-defined binding, or an action command string; nil to remove an override binding. For example:
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_SetOverrideBinding)
declare function SetOverrideBinding(owner: Frame, isPriority: boolean, key: string, command: string)
--- Sets an override binding that performs a button click.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `owner`: The frame this binding "belongs" to; this can later be used to clear all override bindings belonging to a particular frame.
--- - `isPriority`: true if this is a priority binding, false otherwise. Both types of override bindings take precedence over normal bindings.
--- - `key`: Binding to bind the command to. For example, "Q", "ALT-Q", "ALT-CTRL-SHIFT-Q", "BUTTON5"
--- - `buttonName`: Name of the button widget this binding should fire a click event for.
--- - `mouseClick`: Mouse button name argument passed to the OnClick handlers.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_SetOverrideBindingClick)
declare function SetOverrideBindingClick(owner: Frame, isPriority: boolean, key: string, buttonName: string, mouseClick: string?)
